From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:55:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/44] avfilter/deinterlace_v4l2m2m: scale output timestamps
 to the field rate

config_props halves the output time base to carry the doubled frame rate,
but the output frames kept the input timestamps. Every timestamp was
read at half its value, so 25 fps interlaced input played out as 100 fps
instead of 50 fps.

Give the second field twice the input timestamp and the first field the
sum of the previous and current timestamps, the midpoint in the output
time base, and set the frame time base to match.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_v4l2m2m.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_v4l2m2m.c b/libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_v4l2m2m.c
index a25bd55eb8..192d6f9640 100644
--- a/libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_v4l2m2m.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_v4l2m2m.c
@@ -814,11 +814,15 @@ static int deint_v4l2m2m_dequeue(AVFilterContext *avctx, AVFrame *input_frame)
 
     if (ctx->prev_in_frame && ctx->prev_in_frame->pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE
        && input_frame->pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE) {
-      first_pts = (ctx->prev_in_frame->pts + input_frame->pts) / 2;
+      first_pts = ctx->prev_in_frame->pts + input_frame->pts;
       av_log(priv, AV_LOG_DEBUG, "calculated first pts %"PRId64"\n", first_pts);
     }
 
     output_frame_1->pts = first_pts;
+    output_frame_1->time_base = outlink->time_base;
+    if (input_frame->pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE)
+        output_frame_2->pts = input_frame->pts * 2;
+    output_frame_2->time_base = outlink->time_base;
 
     err = ff_filter_frame(outlink, output_frame_1);
     if (err < 0) {
